# rule.always.get-a-second-opinion-before-foreman

> do not knock on the foreman's door until you have phoned a friend.

one peer opinion is owed before any escalation: before `--as blocked` (is it truly a wall?) · before "which do you prefer?" · before you report an undiagnosable defect (ask the role that owns it) · before you label two reviewers irreconcilable (ask a third).

phone the RIGHT friend: implementation/failure modes → **mechanic** · boundaries/decomposition/word choice → **architect** · cli/api/errors/output → **ergonomist** · where a lesson or term belongs → **learner**/**librarian** · testable behavior/criterion/scope → **behaver**.

use `rhx enroll --roles <role>`, then that role's `review`; never a hand-rolled path.

carve-outs: peer genuinely unreachable · wall unambiguously foreman-only (credential/grant) · wisher scope decision. "i was fairly sure" is not one.

blocker: an escalation with no peer sought and no reason recorded · a peer opinion obtained and not cited · a hand-rolled review path.
